# {{.Title}}

A [tifa](https://github.com/liustack/tifa) app: a todo list stored in SQLite.

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `{{.Install}}` | Install the npm packages |
| `go tool tifa dev` | Run the app at http://127.0.0.1:9527, rebuilding on every change |
| `go test ./...` | Test the Go code |
| `{{.Run}} typecheck` | Check the TypeScript |
| `go tool tifa build` | Build the single executable into `bin/` |

- Pages and the code behind them live in `app/`, grouped by domain. `app/todos/todo.go` is the todo list, next to the pages that use it. Add a domain as a folder under `app/`.
- Each folder under `app/` is a URL. `app/todos/todo+/` is `/todos/{todo}`.
- The root folder holds what the whole app shares: `db.go` opens the database, `schema.sql` holds its tables, and `hooks.go` opens the database when the app starts and closes it when it stops.
- The database is `app.db` in the folder the app runs in. Set `DB_PATH` to put it elsewhere.

See [Writing an app](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/app.md) and [Structuring an app](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/structure.md).
